## Naming Conventions

### Backend
| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | camelCase | `orderService.ts` |
| Functions | camelCase | `executeSwap` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `OrderService` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `MAX_SLIPPAGE` |
| Types/Interfaces | PascalCase | `SwapParams` |

### Frontend
| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `SwapForm.tsx` |
| Hooks | useCamelCase | `useTokenPrice.ts` |
| Utilities | camelCase | `formatNumber.ts` |
| Stores | camelCaseStore | `tradingStore.ts` |

---

## Mandatory Requirements

### 1. Tests are Required

Every new feature MUST include tests:
- Backend: Service tests, route tests, WebSocket tests
- Frontend: Component tests, hook tests
- Aim for >80% coverage on new code

### 2. Documentation is Required

Every new feature MUST update documentation:
- New API endpoints
- New WebSocket message types
- New environment variables
- Configuration changes

### 3. Security Review

All features touching user data or funds MUST:
- Validate all inputs
- Implement rate limiting
- Follow non-custodial patterns
- Be reviewed for vulnerabilities

---

## When to Plan vs. Implement Directly

### Use Plan Mode for:
- New trading features (order types, strategies)
- WebSocket protocol changes
- Database schema changes
- Blockchain integration changes
- Security-related changes

### Implement Directly for:
- Bug fixes with clear scope
- UI component updates
- Adding tests to existing code
- Documentation updates
- Performance optimizations with clear metrics

---

## Implementation Checklist

### Before Starting
- [ ] Target area(s) identified (frontend/backend/blockchain)
- [ ] Affected files identified
- [ ] Existing patterns understood
- [ ] API contract defined (for full-stack changes)
- [ ] Security implications considered
- [ ] User approval obtained (for non-trivial changes)

### Before Completing
- [ ] Code implemented and working
- [ ] Follows existing patterns
- [ ] TypeScript types complete (no `any`)
- [ ] Error handling comprehensive
- [ ] Input validation in place
- [ ] **Tests created and passing** (MANDATORY)
- [ ] **Documentation updated** (MANDATORY)
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] Rate limiting applied where needed

